      "sequence": 178,
      "meaning": "The false sage forbids the king to tell this story: if a sixth person hears it, or if it becomes public, or a Brahmin curse falls, destruction is certain; otherwise even the anger of Hari and Śiva cannot kill him. Clasping his feet, the king agrees that no one can withstand the wrath of Brahmin or teacher; a guru can protect from Brahmā’s anger, but no saviour exists for opposition to a guru. The king promises to follow every word, saying only the dreadful Brahmin curse frightens him, and begs the compassionate ascetic—his sole perceived ally—to explain how Brahmins may be brought under control.",
