      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0167",
      "sequence": 179,
      "meaning": "The schemer says that the world has many difficult means whose success is uncertain, but one very easy method has a single problem: it depends on the ascetic visiting the king’s city, though he has never entered anyone’s home or village. If he refuses, the king’s purpose fails, creating a dilemma. The king cites scripture’s teaching that the great lovingly stoop for the small: mountains bear grass on their heads, the unfathomable ocean bears foam on its crest, and the earth continually carries dust. Grasping his feet, he begs the compassionate saint to endure hardship for his sake.",
