    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0168",
      "sequence": 180,
      "meaning": "Knowing the king completely subject to him, the deceitful ascetic promises that nothing is difficult for him and that he will certainly accomplish the work, because Pratāpabhānu is his devotee in mind, body and speech. Yogic methods, austerity and mantra bear fruit only when kept secret. If the ascetic cooks while the king himself serves the meal without anyone knowing the cook, everyone who eats will obey the king; whoever later eats in those diners’ homes will also come under his control. He tells the king to take a yearlong vow: invite one hundred thousand new Brahmins with their families each day, and the ascetic will provide the daily feast for the entire vow.",
