    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0169",
      "sequence": 181,
      "meaning": "In this easy way, says the pretender, every Brahmin will soon submit to the king; their sacrifices and rites will in turn bring the gods under control. He adds one warning: he will not appear in this guise. By māyā he will abduct the royal priest, make himself identical to him, keep the real priest hidden for a year, and, wearing his form, arrange everything. Since much of the night has passed, the king should sleep; the sage will use ascetic power to convey him and his horse home asleep, then arrive in the priest’s guise on the third day. When called alone, he will identify himself and recount the plan.",
